(0-1 T total). Otherwise it is re-expressed as Rz(a) H Rz(b) H Rz(c) (a ZXZ Euler
decomposition), so gridsynth only ever has to pay for at most ONE arbitrary angle per run
instead of the 2-3 arbitrary angles that were there before. This is correct because the run
is exactly the matrix product of its own gates with no entangling gate touching that qubit in
